entric. Candidate C has strongest technical and leadership but biggest adaptability/coop issues. Candidate D has responsibility and problem solving but hot temper.\n\nMaybe the panel might lean to Candidate B because reliability and stress resilience are crucial, and cooperation can be trained? But nasty remarks is serious. Candidate A's communication difficulty may affect crew. Candidate C's unorganized may affect safety. Candidate D's hot temper also serious.\n\nWe need to make a contribution: either support Candidate C, ask for more info, or propose alternative. Since Agent 1 already recommended C, we could either agree and ask for more info, or challenge and propose another candidate. Let's consider: we have facts that Candidate B handles stress very well and is very conscientious, which are key. Also B's weak memory for numbers could affect attention. But maybe less severe than C's unorganized and not open to new ideas. So we could argue that B's strengths in reliability and stress resilience outweigh C's concerns, making B a stronger overall fit. Provide evidence: B very conscientious, handles stress well, good at assessing weather, excellent computer skills. Concern: nasty remarks about colleagues (crew cooperation). We can ask if anyone has observed B's crew cooperation beyond remarks.\n\nThus we can say: I am less convinced by C due to unorganized and not open to new ideas, and propose B as stronger alternative. Provide evidence. Ask panel for observations on B's crew cooperation.\n\nThus our vote: Candidate B.\n\nWe must include METADATA_JSON with vote \"Candidate B\". Provide public message referencing Agent 1's recommendation, our own facts, and request info.\n\nProceed."}
